\tag{fdip}
\title{Dirac–Kähler operators}
\date{2026-11-02}

\p{The [centered Dirac operator](fdip-000T) on a periodic grid has
kernel dimension #{2^{d+e}}, where #{e} counts the even periods.
On a square torus that dimension changes when a side length changes
parity. The operator built from the coboundary does not. On every
square torus the kernel of #{d+d^\dagger} has dimension #{4}.}

\p{The exterior algebra of a free module carries a multiplication and
a contraction for each basis vector. No quadratic form enters those
two operations. Their ordered products are every linear endomorphism
of the algebra, and the sums of matching pairs obey the Clifford
relation of the standard dot product. The following section proves
both statements. The section after it takes up the product of
cochains.}

